<--------------------------- 1. Slurm & Job Management -------------------------->

<--- Submit & Cancel Jobs --->
* touch myscript.sh      : Create a new empty job script.
* sbatch myscript.sh     : Submit a job script to the cluster queue.
* scancel --me           : Cancel ALL your currently running and pending jobs.
* scancel <job_id>       : Cancel a specific job using its ID.
* scancel $(squeue -u $USER -h -o "%i") : A smart command to cancel all your jobs dynamically.

<--- Monitor Jobs --->
* squeue --me            : Show the status of your jobs (or use: squeue -u $USER).
* squeue --me -l         : Show a detailed status of your jobs.
* tail -f <log_file>     : Watch your output log file update in real-time (e.g., tail -f logs/baseline4.txt).

<--- Resources & Nodes --->
* sinfo -Rl              : Show detailed information on cluster nodes (CPU, Memory, Disk states).
* scontrol show job <id> : Show detailed limits and allocations for a specific running job.
* scontrol show job $(squeue -u $USER -h -o "%i") | grep -i cpu : Show exactly how many CPUs are allocated to your current job.
* scontrol show nodes | grep -A5 "NodeName" : Check all nodes for available configurations.

<--- *NEW* Interactive & GPU Monitoring --->
* srun --pty bash        : Start an interactive session on a compute node for quick testing before submitting a batch job.
* srun --jobid=<id> nvidia-smi : Check the real-time GPU memory usage of your running job.


